{
  "_comment": "Piece-level mask manifest. One mask PNG per piece per outfit => white = that piece's pixels, black = everything else. A garment that is present but not visible behind an outer layer still gets a mask file, but z:0 means it is occluded at the edges the recolour can actually reach: the shop should recolour it together with its parent piece instead of independently (the pixels cannot be isolated without guessing). z:1 pieces have clean, independent boundaries.",
  "canvas": {
    "w": 768,
    "h": 1376,
    "masks": "same size, 8-bit PNG, 255=that piece, 0=not",
    "mask_derivation": "derived once from template/base/<ID>.jpg; valid for all six tone folders because every tone file is the identical frame with only skin L/S changed (verified: silhouette IoU vs base >= 0.999, backdrop movement 0.000%)"
  },
